STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    12000, L"This is your last act of defiance! Your Wonder will fall!"
    12001, L"You call THAT a Wonder?  HA!"
    12002, L"I might just knock your 'wondrous' monument down."
    12003, L"That's it, you're toast!"
    12004, L"What goes up... WILL COME DOWN!"
    12005, L"Wow... I'm sooo impressed..."
    12006, L"I tried being reasonable.  You just didn't listen... did you? DID YOU?!?"
    12007, L"Now I must destroy you.  Remember, this was your choice."
    12008, L"Say goodbye to that Wonder."
    12009, L"A Wonder, eh? Wonders burn reeeal good."
END

STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    12100, L"We will help you protect this marvelous creation."
    12101, L"Such a Wonder will surely draw attention.  Help is on the way."
    12102, L"Your creation marks the dawning of a new era.  We shall defend it to the last."
    12103, L"We shall flock to your city to see your great achievement!"
    12104, L"Such a monument will need protection.  Troops are on the way."
    12105, L"You'll need some help defending that."
    12106, L"That is truly a Wonder of the world. "
    12107, L"I 'wonder' how long that will last?  You may need my help."
    12108, L"Very nice... we'll be right over."
    12109, L"Most impressive.  But you'll need more troops than that!  I'm coming."
END

STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    12200, L"I have nothing to offer for your defense, but we're still friends, right?"
    12201, L"Our reserves have run dry. We have nothing to give."
    12202, L"Love to help, but we've recently been decimated. "
    12203, L"We can't offer you anything more than we already have."
    12204, L"You want me to send dead guys?  I got plenty of those."
    12205, L"We're short on troops.  Your Wonder will have to stand without our help."
    12206, L"Holy smokes... that's a wonder alright.  But we haven't enough troops to help."
    12207, L"I hope you have the troops to support that, because we don't."
END

STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    12208, L"Marvelous! Incredible! But I'm afraid you're on your own."
    12209, L"Phew... That must have cost some bucks.  We're short on both cash and troops at the moment."
END

STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    12300, L"Perhaps I could spare some troops... "
    12301, L"Very well. I shall send troops to your aid."
    12302, L"Perfect! Now I can show you how a REAL general fights a battle."
    12303, L"BAM!  Army on its way!"
END

STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    12304, L"I see it.  I'm already on the way."
    12305, L"Who are they kidding?  When I get there, they won't stand a chance!"
    12306, L"Can't handle it by yourself, huh?  Don't worry, I'm here to help you out!"
    12307, L"Oooh, this is going to be fun! "
    12308, L"My army will soon surround them."
    12309, L"My troops are ready - we'll do our best."
END

STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    12330, L"Fire will rain from the skies on our enemies!"
    12331, L"Our Air force is coming in!  Keep your helmets on!"
    12332, L"Air force en route.  It's gonna rain lead!"
    12333, L"Winging in! My Air Force is in action!"
    12334, L"Our planes are coming in now."
    12335, L"Roger.  Squadron on the way."
END

STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    12336, L"We'll do a fly by!"
    12337, L"10-4! We're on our way!"
    12338, L"I'll send my Air Force.  The pilots are ready to go."
    12339, L"I see... it's up to me now.  Thanks."
END

STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    12360, L"My warships are en route."
    12361, L"I've gotta fleet with your name on it!"
    12362, L"Shipping out!"
    12363, L"Avast ye lan' lubbers! Help's comin'!"
    12364, L"Aye Aye, Captain! Ships are coming!"
    12365, L"Just rounding up the last sailors on shore leave and we'll raise anchor."
    12366, L"We'll sink the sea dogs!"
    12367, L"All our ships are on the way."
END

STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    12368, L"Sounds good, I like to sink things."
    12369, L"Their ships will soon be on the bottom!"
END

STRINGTABLE
BEGIN
    12400, L"I can spare no more troops."
    12401, L"I hope you're not talking to me - I've got nothing to send."
    12402, L"You want me to attack them? With what!?"
    12403, L"I'm all flared out right now."
    12404, L"I'm sorry, all lines are currently busy, but if you'd like to leave a message..."
    12405, L"I can't send any troops, but I'm thinking really positive thoughts for you."
    12406, L"Thanks for holding, your flare is important to us!"
    12407, L"Sorry, I've got nothing over here.  Can't we all just get along?"
    12408, L"I can't help and I'm fresh out of excuses."
    12409, L"I'm afraid you're on your own.  "
END

